---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout title="Cybersecurity" description="Blue Team, Security Operations, Network Security, and the connection between technical controls and business risk.">
  <section class="about-intro cyber-hero" aria-labelledby="cyber-hero-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Cybersecurity · Professional Development</p>
    <h2 id="cyber-hero-heading">Understanding the systems. Recognizing the risks. Strengthening the response.</h2>
    <p class="lead">I am developing practical cybersecurity capabilities with an immediate focus on Blue Team and Security Operations. My background in business operations, client services, systems coordination, and cybersecurity services gives me a useful perspective on how security work connects to the organizations it protects.</p>
    <p>My current learning priorities include security monitoring, threat detection, network analysis, incident response, and the operational discipline needed to document, investigate, and communicate security issues.</p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/xxReina-28">Explore GitHub</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ninasuico/">Connect on LinkedIn</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="direction-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">01 · Direction</p>
    <h2 id="direction-heading">Career focus</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-3">
      <article class="card cyber-card cyber-card--blue">
        <h3>Blue Team &amp; SOC</h3>
        <p class="muted">Immediate development focus</p>
        <p>Security monitoring, alert triage, threat detection, investigation, incident documentation, and response fundamentals.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card cyber-card cyber-card--aqua">
        <h3>Network Security</h3>
        <p class="muted">Technical foundation</p>
        <p>Networking concepts, traffic inspection, infrastructure security, vulnerability awareness, and defensive tooling.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card cyber-card cyber-card--violet">
        <h3>GRC &amp; Security Strategy</h3>
        <p class="muted">Longer-term specialization</p>
        <p>Risk assessment, control objectives, governance, compliance, security policies, and translating technical risk into business decisions.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="credentials-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">02 · Education</p>
    <h2 id="credentials-heading">Training &amp; credentials</h2>
    <div class="credential-grid">
      <article class="credential-item glass-surface cyber-credential">
        <span class="credential-mark" aria-hidden="true">G</span>
        <div class="credential-copy">
          <h3>Google Cybersecurity Professional Certificate</h3>
          <p class="muted">Google · Coursera · Completed November 8, 2026</p>
          <p>Completed the nine-course professional certificate covering security foundations, risk, networks, Linux, SQL, security tools, assets and vulnerabilities, detection and response, and Python automation.</p>
          <span class="status-label">Completed</span>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="credential-item glass-surface cyber-credential">
        <span class="credential-mark" aria-hidden="true">R</span>
        <div class="credential-copy">
          <h3>Cybersecurity Bootcamp</h3>
          <p class="muted">RivanCyber Institute · October 13–16, 2026</p>
          <p>Instructor-led foundational training with practical exposure to defensive security concepts, security tools, labs, and risk-related topics.</p>
          <span class="status-label">Completed training</span>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="credential-item glass-surface cyber-credential">
        <span class="credential-mark" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        <div class="credential-copy">
          <h3>CompTIA Security+ (SY0-701)</h3>
          <p class="muted">CompTIA</p>
          <p>Preparing for the certification examination. This is a learning milestone, not a certification claim.</p>
          <span class="status-label">Exam preparation</span>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="labs-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">03 · Practical learning</p>
    <h2 id="labs-heading">Technical labs &amp; learning repositories</h2>
    <p class="lead">These repositories preserve my training notes, exercises, and technical explorations. They are learning evidence, not claims of professional production experience.</p>
    <div class="grid grid-3">
      <article class="card cyber-repo">
        <h3>Security+ Bootcamp Notes</h3>
        <p>Course notes and lab references covering security foundations, risk management, defensive concepts, Azure security, MITRE ATT&amp;CK, and secure coding.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/xxReina-28/RivanSecPlus701">View RivanSecPlus701</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card cyber-repo">
        <h3>Network &amp; Infrastructure Labs</h3>
        <p>Networking exercises, routing and DNS notes, infrastructure configuration examples, and introductory automation scripts.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/xxReina-28/SECplus701">View SECplus701</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card cyber-repo">
        <h3>Security+ Learning Reference</h3>
        <p>A structured study reference used to reinforce Security+ concepts and prepare for the certification examination.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/xxReina-28/CompTIA-Security-SY0-701-Full-Training-Guide">View training guide</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="tooling-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">04 · Tool exposure</p>
    <h2 id="tooling-heading">Tools &amp; environments explored</h2>
    <p>My current hands-on learning includes introductory use and exploration of the following tools. Familiarity is developing and should not be read as production-level proficiency.</p>
    <ul class="badges" aria-label="Tools explored">
      {['Wazuh', 'Wireshark', 'Nmap', 'Kali Linux', 'TryHackMe', 'Linux', 'SQL', 'Python'].map((tool) => <li class="badge">{tool}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="transfer-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">05 · Professional foundation</p>
    <h2 id="transfer-heading">What I bring from business operations</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-3">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Operational discipline</h3>
        <p>Experience documenting workflows, coordinating handoffs, maintaining records, and following issues through to resolution.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Risk-aware coordination</h3>
        <p>Exposure to cybersecurity services, fintech operations, compliance-related workflows, and cross-functional business priorities.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Business communication</h3>
        <p>Ability to translate operational issues, technical inputs, and management requirements into clear documentation and actionable next steps.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="roadmap-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">06 · Next milestones</p>
    <h2 id="roadmap-heading">Development roadmap</h2>
    <ol class="method-sequence">
      <li class="method-step glass-surface">
        <span class="method-index">01 · NOW</span>
        <h3>Strengthen foundations</h3>
        <p>Complete Security+ preparation and continue structured networking, Linux, and security fundamentals practice.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="method-step glass-surface">
        <span class="method-index">02 · NEXT</span>
        <h3>Build SOC evidence</h3>
        <p>Develop documented alert-triage, log-analysis, detection, and incident-response labs with repeatable steps and evidence.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="method-step glass-surface">
        <span class="method-index">03 · LATER</span>
        <h3>Develop risk &amp; controls depth</h3>
        <p>Build practical risk registers, control mappings, assessment reports, and governance case studies grounded in recognized frameworks.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section narrative-panel glass-surface" aria-labelledby="disclosure-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Evidence standard</p>
    <h2 id="disclosure-heading">Learning honestly. Demonstrating clearly.</h2>
    <p>This portfolio distinguishes completed training, guided coursework, independent labs, proposed work, and verified professional outcomes. Tools listed here reflect learning exposure unless a project provides evidence of a deeper level of implementation. No employer systems, confidential information, or production data are included.</p>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
